# =============================================================================
# MaburVM — PRODUCTION environment example (.env.production.example)
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy to `.env.production` and EDIT every value. This file ships with EMPTY
# (guarded) mandatory values — NOT working placeholders. Every line marked `:?`
# in docker-compose.production.yml REFUSES to start if the variable is unset or
# empty, so a deploy can never succeed with a blank. Replace each empty value
# with a real one before `up`.
#
# SECRETS ARE NOT HERE. The PostgreSQL password and the panel's RESTRICTED S3
# credentials are read from host files via the compose `secrets:` block:
#
#   install -m 0400 -o root /path/to/password.txt deploy/secrets/postgres_password
#   install -m 0400 -o root /path/to/s3pass.txt   deploy/secrets/s3_restricted_password
#
# Secret source-file guidance (host-side bind mount, NOT a managed store):
#   * mode 0400, owned by root (or the user running `docker compose`).
#   * The container's ROOT entrypoint/init reads them before dropping privileges,
#     so they do NOT need to be world-readable. Do NOT use a 0444 workaround.
#   * Prefer writing each secret precisely. The official postgres entrypoint reads
#     the file via command substitution (strips a terminal newline) and our panel
#     app resolver also trims surrounding whitespace, so a trailing newline is NOT
#     preserved as part of the secret. Still, write exactly the secret you intend.
#   * Never commit deploy/secrets/ (a .gitignore rule covers it).
#
# TLS / PROXY: Only the web UI port is published (loopback by default). Put a
# reverse proxy (Caddy / nginx / Traefik) in FRONT of web to terminate TLS.
# Do NOT expose the panel API, PostgreSQL, MinIO, or the agent.
#
# IMAGE TAG REVIEW / SBOM / CVE: Before each deploy, confirm every image tag
# (postgres:16.14, minio/minio:RELEASE.2025-09-07T16-13-09Z, node:22.23.1-
# alpine3.24, alpine:3.24) is the exact version you intend. `latest` is never
# used. Docker image build/start and runtime tests remain release gates (NOT
# executed as part of writing this file).
# =============================================================================

# --- Release images --------------------------------------------------------------
# Empty: panel and web are built on this host from the checkout (maburvm-*:local).
# Set both to run a published release instead, e.g.
#   MABURVM_IMAGE_PREFIX=ghcr.io/OWNER/maburvm
#   MABURVM_VERSION=v1.2.0
# then `docker compose ... pull panel web && docker compose ... up -d --no-build`.
# scripts/upgrade-panel.sh --version vX.Y.Z changes MABURVM_VERSION for you.
#MABURVM_IMAGE_PREFIX=
#MABURVM_VERSION=

# --- Web UI port (published on loopback; proxy it behind TLS) ------------------
WEB_PORT=3000

# --- Database connection -------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret DB identity (used by both PostgreSQL and the panel).
POSTGRES_USER=maburvm
POSTGRES_DB=maburvm
# The DB PASSWORD comes from deploy/secrets/postgres_password (compose secret).
#
# DB_SSL_MODE for the SELF-CONTAINED internal Postgres defaults to `disable`
# (the stock postgres image has SSL OFF). If you point DB_HOST at a REMOTE or
# MANAGED Postgres, `disable` is incorrect: you need real server certs + client
# config, which is a separately validated connection design — set DB_SSL_MODE
# accordingly and verify the cert chain out of band.
DB_SSL_MODE=disable

# --- Object storage (MinIO, in-cluster) ---------------------------------------
# MinIO ROOT credentials (confined to minio + minio-init ONLY). MinIO does NOT
# support reliable *_FILE indirection for root creds across versions, so these
# MUST be real, non-placeholder values. We do NOT use unverified secret-file
# behavior for MinIO root configuration.
MINIO_ROOT_USER=
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=
# Bucket the panel uses (created by minio-init). Non-secret.
S3_BUCKET=maburvm
# Restricted S3 user identity (non-secret) created by minio-init for the panel.
# Defaults to maburvm-app-v1 on a clean install. Its PASSWORD is the FILE secret
# deploy/secrets/s3_restricted_password. Never set this to the MinIO root user.
MINIO_S3_USER=maburvm-app-v1
#
# Backup object-storage transport flags consumed by the agent
# (internal/agent/server/node_agent.go) and the River worker
# (internal/shared/queue/workers.go) via STORAGE_*/S3_*. The panel's
# internal/panel/storage/s3.go reads S3_* for config validation but is NOT a
# production backup-transport consumer. Backups of customers' VMs do not use
# these: their destination is set in the panel (Settings, System, Backup) and
# must be a store the nodes can reach, which this MinIO is not.
# List them here for clarity. Do NOT set S3_ENDPOINT with a scheme (use
# `minio:9000`), and enable HTTP + path-style for the in-cluster MinIO:
#   S3_ENDPOINT=minio:9000
#   S3_FORCE_HTTP=true
#   S3_USE_PATH_STYLE=true
#   S3_ACCESS_KEY=maburvm-app-v1
#   S3_SECRET_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/s3_restricted_password
# (The production compose already sets these for the panel service.)

# --- Public panel URL ---------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public HTTPS URL of the panel (e.g. https://panel.example.com). Used
# by node installer scripts (/install-agent.sh) to build their embedded download
# URL behind the reverse proxy — NOT the internal URL. Required. Only the
# starting value: once an address is saved under System settings, Panel, that
# one is used (as are the billing, SSO and metrics values saved there).
PANEL_PUBLIC_URL=

# --- CORS / allowed origins ----------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of the exact origin(s) your web UI is served from, e.g.
# https://panel.example.com  (no trailing slash). Never use * in production.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# --- Optional: trusted proxies -------------------------------------------------
# IPs/CIDRs whose X-Forwarded-For the panel believes when it works out a
# client's address (sign-in rate limit, per-user IP allow-lists, audit log).
# Unset trusts loopback and private ranges, which is right for the reference
# setup (Caddy on the host -> web -> panel on the compose network). Set it when
# a proxy in front of you has a public address. A bad entry stops the panel
# from starting.
#TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# --- Optional: billing system ---------------------------------------------------
# The billing webhook (POST /webhooks/billing) lets a billing system such as
# WHMCS create, suspend, resize and remove VMs. It is OFF, and answers 503,
# until BOTH values are set. Enter the same two values in the billing system's
# server settings (integrations/whmcs/README.md). Generate each with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`; the panel's security check flags anything shorter
# than 24 characters. Whoever holds them can create and destroy VMs. Both can
# be set under System settings, Panel instead (stored encrypted); a value saved
# there takes over from these at once.
BILLING_API_KEY=
BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Transfer quotas. Plans carry a monthly quota and what happens past it
# (throttle, stop, or bill the overage). With anything but "true" here the
# panel only MEASURES: nobody is throttled or stopped. Once on, a VM is acted
# on at the moment it crosses its quota; one that already crossed this month
# while this was off is left alone until the next month. This is only the
# starting value: once the switch is saved under System settings, Quotas, the
# saved value decides.
BANDWIDTH_ENFORCE=false
# Rescue mode boots this ISO (an http(s) URL each node downloads, or the full
# path of an ISO already on every node) until one is saved under System
# settings, Rescue. Left empty with nothing saved there, customers are told
# rescue mode is not available.
RESCUE_ISO_URL=

# --- Optional: externally managed object storage -------------------------------
# Using an EXTERNAL S3 store is NOT an env-only switch in this file — it requires
# a separately authored Compose model (different S3_ENDPOINT/creds, the `minio`
# and `minio-init` services omitted or replaced) with its own validation. If you
# do that, set S3_ENDPOINT + S3_ACCESS_KEY/S3_SECRET_KEY accordingly there.

# --- Panel backups (panel-backup service) --------------------------------------
# The panel-backup service uploads a nightly encrypted backup of the panel
# database and its secrets.json to storage OFF this host. It does nothing, and
# says so in its log, until BOTH values below are set. Setup, restore and the
# restore rehearsal: docs/DEPLOYMENT.md section 9.
#
# Where to upload: an rclone destination ("remote:bucket/path"). The remote is
# defined in deploy/secrets/rclone.conf (mode 0600). Not the bundled MinIO: it
# is on this host and is lost with it. A plain path is refused for the same reason.
BACKUP_DEST=
# age PUBLIC key(s) the backups are encrypted to (age1..., comma separated).
# Generate the pair on another machine with `age-keygen`. The private key must
# never be on this host or in the backup destination.
BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENTS=
# Backups older than this many days are deleted after each successful upload.
# 0 keeps everything (for storage that expires objects itself).
BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Daily backup time, HH:MM in UTC.
BACKUP_TIME=02:30
# Optional: a URL fetched after each successful backup, for a monitor that
# alerts when the nightly fetch stops arriving.
BACKUP_HEARTBEAT_URL=

# --- Upgrades ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each migration gets this long at boot (a Go duration). Raise it before an
# upgrade whose notes mention a long migration on a large table.
MIGRATION_TIMEOUT=30m
# When set (e.g. 6h), the panel refuses to apply pending migrations unless
# scripts/upgrade-panel.sh recorded a database dump within that time, so an
# upgrade started any other way cannot migrate without a way back. Empty: off.
MIGRATION_REQUIRE_BACKUP_WITHIN=
